Subject: [PATCH] PR #49182: Check scatter carry predicate replication before
 all-reduce motion
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Imported from GitHub PR https://github.com/openxla/xla/pull/49182

📝 Summary of Changes
Fixes #49143.

Reuse the existing generic buffer-use checker `existing is_buffer_used` and remove the weaker scatter-only helper `IsScatterBufferUsed`. Unsafe scatter patterns keep their all-reduce inside the loop.

Added eight parameterized minimal-HLO regression cases that check whether the pass hoists the all-reduce or retains it inside the loop. And the tests ran on CPU host.

🎯 Justification
The scatter-specific path in `while-loop-all-reduce-code-motion` accepts a select between carry and zero without checking whether its predicate is replicated within the all-reduce group. Hoisting the collective while retaining a select such as `partition_id == 0 ? carry : 0` discards earlier contributions on nonzero partitions.

🚀 Kind of Contribution
🐛 Bug Fix, 🧪 Tests

🧪 Unit Tests
```bash
bazel test \
  //xla/hlo/transforms/collectives:while_loop_all_reduce_code_motion_test \
  //xla/hlo/transforms/collectives:while_loop_all_reduce_code_motion_setup_test
```

| Tests | Before fix | After fix |
|---|---|---|
| Eight new regression cases | 4 passed, 4 failed | 8 passed |

The four failing cases previously hoisted the collective despite a device-dependent predicate. After the fix, it remains inside the loop; the four positive controls still pass.

